item.text:
{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Tier-1 source owner for bounded work: steps, transitions, intake, admission, applicability, configurations and delegation; context construction, acquisition, activation and derived-surface currency; result refinements and disposition; totality, refinement and licensing; work state, restart, proportionality and closed-result reuse. Its statements describe the subject methodology, not authority for this interpretation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":14,
          "quote":"Tier 1. Owns how bounded work proceeds:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key":"activation_standard",
      "label":"ACTIVATION"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Activation of one reference frame or one declared active frame configuration on an exact subject. Context is the activated frame's projection to the actor. Intake, admission, applicability and activation remain distinct relations even within one invocation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":37,
          "quote":"A step is the activation of one reference frame, or one declared active\nframe configuration, on an exact subject",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step",
          "start_line":32
        }
      ],
      "key":"step",
      "label":"Step"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A bounded change from current state to next state performed by one step. Current state includes the material workspace, authoritative inputs, justified knowledge and explicit unknowns. Its account is distinct from the state. Work fitting one activation is one transition; larger work is refined into bounded transitions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":137,
          "quote":"A transition is a bounded change from the current state to a next state,\ncarried out by one step.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions",
          "start_line":133
        }
      ],
      "key":"transition",
      "label":"Transition and current state"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Owner-defined selected outcome, acceptance conditions and governing obligations, expressed as constraints admitting several realised states. In construction it is Z, a predicate over realised states supplied by the governing specification: the selected WHAT across Intent, Product and Specification; descriptions refine Z.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":131,
          "quote":"The destination is defined by constraints:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FTransitions",
          "start_line":127
        },
        {
          "end_line":219,
          "quote":"The\ngoverning specification, the selected WHAT across the Intent, Product and\nSpecification of the Product that owns the work, supplies Z;",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
          "start_line":216
        }
      ],
      "key":"destination",
      "label":"Destination Z"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The source-owned relation connecting current state A, destination Z, strategy, composition, feedback, correction and evidence-based completion. Three subject accounts are distinct: specification states required conditions; observations describe what holds; causal or predictive models explain possible action effects. A composition boundary connects successive step output and starting state and differs from a categorical join. Feedback includes observation, comparison, diagnosis, authorised response, action and subsequent observation; homeostasis is correction toward requirements, without a convergence or adequacy guarantee.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":207,
          "quote":"This subsection states the construction relation for this corpus:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
          "start_line":200
        },
        {
          "end_line":237,
          "quote":"The specification is the internal reference model of the required\nconditions. Observations describe what does hold.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
          "start_line":231
        }
      ],
      "key":"construction_relation",
      "label":"Construction relation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The reconstructable execution intake naming the governed question, exact subject and basis, permitted inputs, evaluation and result algebra, affected relations and invariants, relied-on transformation admissions, shared machinery bindings, authority and operation grant, actor envelopes, invalidation and re-entry conditions, and conditional cost allowance and measurement.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":358,
          "quote":"A step is activated from an intake sufficient to reconstruct its governing\nrelations without conversation history, commentary or a prior actor's memory",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FIntake",
          "start_line":356
        }
      ],
      "key":"intake",
      "label":"Intake"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Smallest coherent causal dependency cone capable of delivering working behaviour while preserving every affected governing relation. It is the seed set Z of context construction; its projection is context. This seed-set Z is distinct from construction's destination predicate Z.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":405,
          "quote":"The execution unit is the smallest coherent causal dependency cone capable\nof delivering working behaviour while preserving every affected governing\nrelation.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FExecution%20unit",
          "start_line":397
        },
        {
          "end_line":405,
          "quote":"The cone is the seed set Z of §2; the context is its projection.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FExecution%20unit",
          "start_line":405
        }
      ],
      "key":"execution_unit",
      "label":"Execution unit"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Admission validates an exact execution contract against its cited outcome, prerequisite or experiment basis without admitting that basis. Drafting and admission are distinct relations. Contract states include at least drafted, admitted, rejected and superseded; admission evidence identifies mechanism, authority, exact contract identity or digest, decision and evidence including any override.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":413,
          "quote":"Drafting a step's contract and admitting it are distinct relations, even\ninside one invocation that drafts, validates, admits and executes;",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FAdmission",
          "start_line":409
        }
      ],
      "key":"admission",
      "label":"Execution-contract admission"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Evaluation of the predicate that a frame obligation applies to an exact subject, as determined by owning evaluation and scope declarations. Applicability results are distinct from the obligation's evaluation. Exclusion is the obligation's non-result state following falsified applicability; unresolved applicability is not exclusion.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":479,
          "quote":"Deciding applicability is an evaluation of the\npredicate \"the obligation applies to the exact subject\"",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FApplicability",
          "start_line":476
        }
      ],
      "key":"applicability",
      "label":"Applicability and exclusion"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Candidate plus step-produced judgments and evidence, residuals, observations, authority decisions, provenance and exactly one construction-availability stop state. The actor's internal path is outside the output and outside the governed work boundary.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":508,
          "quote":"The step's output is a candidate plus its step-produced facts: judgments with\ntheir evidence, residuals, observations, authority decisions, provenance, and\none stop state, a value of construction availability (§3).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FOutput",
          "start_line":503
        }
      ],
      "key":"step_output",
      "label":"Step output"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Task-wide allocation of responsibilities and information exchanges to frames; activation binds actors to frames. The active frame configuration is the part used for one evaluation or decision. Allocation depends on operations, dependencies, available actor capabilities and required assurance. Reconfiguration is any change of allocation during work. A coordinator, where selected to separate task construction from delivery management, retains the longer-term outcome.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":516,
          "quote":"A configuration allocates a task's responsibilities and information\nexchanges to frames; activation binds an actor to each frame (§2).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConfiguration",
          "start_line":512
        }
      ],
      "key":"configuration",
      "label":"Configuration"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Roles are configurable relations over steps, not actor kinds or a fixed inventory. When their operations occur, a constructor owns bounded implementation and self-review, an assessor independently evaluates a frozen candidate, and a decision owner disposes. A bounded proxy is an existing grant-bound delegation, not authority conferred by a role name.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":649,
          "quote":"Roles are relations over steps that a configuration allocates\n(Configuration above), not kinds of actor and not a fixed inventory.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation",
          "start_line":635
        }
      ],
      "key":"roles_and_delegation",
      "label":"Roles and delegation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Source-defined procedure taking seed set Z, material dependency relation family R and actor envelope B: compute exact finite unique material closure, project it with recorded boundary seams, test fit, and acquire exact declared inputs. Activation binds reusable frame declarations to exact subject and basis; evaluation applies declared invariants, evidence rules and result algebra. Acquisition is read-only observation within intake permissions, not admission or a new actor stage. A prompt is rendered contract over typed authority, not source law.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":713,
          "quote":"Given a seed set Z (the subject, outcome and affected relations named in the\nintake), a relation family R (the dependency relations whose change can\nalter the result, basis validity, evidence sufficiency or authority), and\nthe actor's envelope B:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope",
          "start_line":710
        }
      ],
      "key":"context_construction",
      "label":"Context construction, acquisition and activation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Material derived from named owning sources by copying, projection or compression, including projected task frames and, where a current a_c interpretation exists, its task constraint surface. It owns no determination and has no universal sufficiency claim.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":806,
          "quote":"A derived surface is material derived from owning\nsources by copying, projection or compression, such as a projected frame\nfor a task; it names its sources and owns no determination.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope",
          "start_line":800
        }
      ],
      "key":"derived_surface",
      "label":"Derived surface"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Selected-basis-relative currency of any derived surface, across methods and carriers. Currency requires every named source identity to equal that source's selected-basis identity; a change to any named source makes the surface stale. Currency, fidelity and question-specific sufficiency are distinct.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":924,
          "quote":"It is current for a selected basis only while every source identity it\n  names equals the identity of that source in the selected basis. A change\n  to any of them makes it stale.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F2.%20Context%20construction%20under%20an%20envelope%2FStaleness%20of%20derived%20surfaces",
          "start_line":912
        }
      ],
      "key":"derived_surface_currency",
      "label":"Derived-surface currency"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Five predicate-specific refinements of the source's core algebra: lawful admission and activation; candidate availability; candidate acceptance at its declared boundary; declared ambiguity resolved on exact basis; intended external effect occurred. Each performed evaluation independently returns one core value with its predicate and domain outcome; unperformed evaluation has no result.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":955,
          "quote":"This section owns them as five\nrefinements of the core.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition",
          "start_line":950
        }
      ],
      "key":"step_result_refinements",
      "label":"Step result refinements"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Pre-step outcome domain for the predicate 'the step is lawfully admitted and activated on the exact subject and basis': activated, admission_refused(authority), admission_refused(basis), closure_unresolved, out_of_frame and cause-bearing activation_refusal. Causes select values; frame activation causes and mappings remain owned by REFERENCE_FRAME §5.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":985,
          "quote":"A step exists only after its contract is admitted (§1, Admission) and its\nframe is activated on the exact subject and basis (§2).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FAdmission%20and%20activation",
          "start_line":975
        }
      ],
      "key":"admission_activation_outcome",
      "label":"Admission and activation outcomes"
    },
    {
      "conditions":["Lawful activation has occurred."],
      "definition":"Total exclusive stop domain for 'a candidate is available': candidate_ready, refused, incomplete, re_entry_requested(authority), re_entry_requested(basis). A constructing step's candidate is its constructed subject; an assessing step's candidate is its closed results. Availability says nothing by itself about fitness or acceptance.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1014,
          "quote":"Construction availability records whether that output\nexists",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FConstruction%20availability",
          "start_line":1012
        }
      ],
      "key":"construction_availability",
      "label":"Construction availability"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Decision owner's acceptance result for an assessed candidate at its declared boundary, with four semantic dispositions: accept, local_repair, re_enter and reject. It consumes but remains separate from candidate availability and assessment results; an assessor's recommendation is evidence, never disposition.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1066,
          "quote":"The disposition is the\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\nresults and stays separate from both",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FDisposition",
          "start_line":1062
        }
      ],
      "key":"candidate_disposition",
      "label":"Candidate disposition"
    },
    {
      "conditions":["An ambiguity is declared."],
      "definition":"Recorded outcome domain resolved, carried, escalated or blocked, mapped for 'the declared ambiguity is resolved on the exact basis'. A carried or blocked ambiguity is known to be open, not an undecidable predicate.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1102,
          "quote":"A declared ambiguity is resolved, carried, escalated or blocked, and the\noutcome is recorded either way",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FAmbiguity%20outcome",
          "start_line":1097
        }
      ],
      "key":"ambiguity_outcome",
      "label":"Ambiguity outcome"
    },
    {
      "conditions":["A step has an intended external effect."],
      "definition":"Evidence-selected outcome domain completed, not_effected or completion_unknown for the intended effect's declared outcome. Whether the effect has ended is a separate question, required conjunctively for completed. Uncertain completion includes completion_unknown and not_effected whose end is not established.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1128,
          "quote":"An effectful step's intended external effect has one of three values,\nmapped for the predicate \"the intended effect occurred\"",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FEffects",
          "start_line":1124
        }
      ],
      "key":"effect_outcome",
      "label":"External-effect outcome and end"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Advance declaration of next moves for every admitted non-satisfied condition class, including unknown: supported continuation within contract, refinement, recovery, yield, owner re-entry or termination. Hard stops remain mandatory regardless of ambiguity risk appetite; reconfiguration responds to the result's cause.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1181,
          "quote":"Each admitted condition class has a declared\nnext move, including an explicit unknown class.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement",
          "start_line":1176
        }
      ],
      "key":"total_handling",
      "label":"Total handling and hard stops"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Refinement decomposes an outer transformation T: A → X into typed steps carrying successive success predicates. Rewriting replaces representation, step or composite with another claimed to preserve meaning. A licensing law is the subject owner's declared law permitting the change. Exact steps preserve declared meaning; approximate steps require an adequacy relation and an argued composite end-to-end deviation bound. Faithful refinement requires exact steps.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1253,
          "quote":"A rewrite step replaces a representation, a step or\na composite by another that is claimed to keep its meaning",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FRefinement",
          "start_line":1245
        },
        {
          "end_line":1264,
          "quote":"Faithful refinement, defined above, requires exact\nsteps.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FRefinement",
          "start_line":1263
        }
      ],
      "key":"refinement",
      "label":"Refinement, rewrite and licensing"
    },
    {
      "conditions":["A transition is material."],
      "definition":"Each admission owner's independent derivation and validation of the complete enclosing relation from authoritative inputs, including every participant and equality join whose identity, validity, authority, currentness or transition can affect or be affected by admission. The transition is admitted as one semantic commit on one exact admission-valid basis or not admitted at all.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1302,
          "quote":"For a material transition, each admission owner is independently\nresponsible for deriving and validating the complete enclosing relation\nfrom authoritative inputs",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FComplete%20enclosing-relation%20admission",
          "start_line":1293
        }
      ],
      "key":"enclosing_relation_admission",
      "label":"Complete enclosing-relation admission"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Qualification of the admission law instantiated for every admission owner and supported boundary declared by accepted design, with case applicability determined by supported inputs, states and operating or threat model. Required forms include direct, supported composite or nested, forged, ambiguous, stale or advanced, incoherent multi-owner, competing authority, fresh reconstruction, exact replay and atomic publication failure.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1353,
          "quote":"Qualification of the admission law is instantiated for every admission\nowner and supported boundary declared by accepted design",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F4.%20Totality%20and%20refinement%2FStanding%20structural%20qualification",
          "start_line":1346
        }
      ],
      "key":"structural_qualification",
      "label":"Standing structural qualification"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Persistent-workspace object comprising governing basis, applicable closed results and judgments with invalidators, residuals and uncertainty over external effects. Resumption re-enters the same method on current material work state, possibly with another actor. Acceptance checkpoint, preservation checkpoint and restart are distinct. Progress categories are accepted movement, prerequisite work, evidence without new progress, churn and forecast revision; these are semantic categories, not a numeric algorithm.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1386,
          "quote":"Work state is the tuple of: the current persistent workspace; the governing\nbasis; the applicable closed results and judgments with their invalidators;\nthe residuals; and the known uncertainty over external effects.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F5.%20Work%20state%20and%20restart",
          "start_line":1379
        }
      ],
      "key":"work_state",
      "label":"Work state, restart and progress"
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["activation_standard"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":28,
          "quote":"it redefines nothing those\nmembers own.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION",
          "start_line":24
        }
      ],
      "key":"activation_ownership_boundary",
      "statement":"ACTIVATION uses FOUNDATIONS §2 objects and §4 result algebra and REFERENCE_FRAME frame objects and activate outcomes without redefining their ownership. An `rc.2 RF #anchor` route denotes stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md and is provenance only.",
      "uncertainty":"Referenced owners are not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["step","construction_relation"],
      "conditions":["Construction is delegated to a probabilistic or agentic worker."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":48,
          "quote":"The\nnormative relation runs: accepted governing basis; bounded affected\nrelation set; selected computational relations; delegated execution and\ndecision authority; construction and self-review; independent live-surface\nassessment where required; one of accept, local repair, re-enter or reject\n(§3); the exact accepted checkpoint; the next already-authorised bounded\naction (§5).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step",
          "start_line":42
        }
