      "key":"progress_categories_and_protocol_falsifiers",
      "statement":"Progress is accepted material movement toward selected outcome. Prerequisite work names enabled obligation; preservation and repeated proof are evidence without new progress; rejected/superseded construction is churn; discovery of hidden distance revises forecast, not negative progress. Paperwork, code volume and test/commit/review counts alone are not progress. Consumer projections are permitted; finer categories must cite this owner and map each to progress, prerequisite, evidence without new progress, churn or forecast revision; unmappable category requires owner change, not parallel category. Execution protocol is false for unreconstructable context; constructor report replacing required independent live evidence; proxy changing governing relations beyond delegation; unrelated incompleteness blocking closed cone; same-process test purportedly proving materially cross-process authority; or rejected activity reported as accepted progress.",
